  "body": "Inspired by @emilio's code review comment.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-popover-algorithm\r\n\r\nWhen hide an auto popover, it calls [hide all popovers until](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-all-popovers-until), which could show other auto popover in the script, which hide the auto popover, on and on.\r\n\r\n```\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<div id='popover1' style=\"top:10px;\" popover=\"auto\">\r\n    <p>This is popover1</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id='popover2' popover=\"auto\">\r\n    <p>This is a popover2</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<script>\r\npopover1.showPopover();\r\npopover1.addEventListener('beforetoggle', (e) => {\r\n    if (e.newState != \"open\") {\r\n        popover2.showPopover();\r\n    }\r\n});\r\nsetTimeout(() => {\r\n    popover1.hidePopover();\r\n}, 1000);\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nhttps://jsbin.com/podukazawu/edit?html,js,output\r\n\r\nMaybe we should introduce element a status, something like `in-hiding-popover`, to prevent this circle?\r\n@emilio @nt1m @jakearchibald @mfreed7 @josepharhar \r\n",
